<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of the Static-Inference Witness Tension</h2>

<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A predictor <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}\in\mathcal{H}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}\in\mathcal{H}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> applies a single computation rule under frozen inference (no instance-wise routing). Fix graph operators <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathrm{L}}(G),T_{\mathrm{H}}(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathrm{L}}(G),T_{\mathrm{H}}(G)</annotation></semantics></math> that decompose node features into complementary components <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\mathrm{L}}:=T_{\mathrm{L}}(G)X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\mathrm{L}}:=T_{\mathrm{L}}(G)X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\mathrm{H}}:=T_{\mathrm{H}}(G)X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\mathrm{H}}:=T_{\mathrm{H}}(G)X</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathrm{L}}(G)+T_{\mathrm{H}}(G)=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathrm{L}}(G)+T_{\mathrm{H}}(G)=I</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., low-/high-pass filters). The witness subfamily <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{1}^{\mathrm{wit}}\subseteq\mathcal{H}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>wit</mi></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{1}^{\mathrm{wit}}\subseteq\mathcal{H}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> consists of static predictors</p>
<table id="A1.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(24)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}(G,X)\ :=\ h_{\theta}\!\big(X_{\mathrm{L}}+\eta_{\theta}X_{\mathrm{H}}\big),\qquad\eta_{\theta}\geq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}(G,X)\ :=\ h_{\theta}\!\big(X_{\mathrm{L}}+\eta_{\theta}X_{\mathrm{H}}\big),\qquad\eta_{\theta}\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed after training and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is the task head. Throughout this appendix we specialize the perturbation set to feature perturbations only (structure budget <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{s}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{s}=0</annotation></semantics></math>), with admissible set <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(G,X):=\{X^{\prime}:(G,X^{\prime})\in B((G,X))\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(G,X):=\{X^{\prime}:(G,X^{\prime})\in B((G,X))\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_smallcaps ltx_title_theorem">Assumption 1 (High-component necessity and perturbations).</h6>
<div id="Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. There exist a reference distribution <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(G,X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(G,X)</annotation></semantics></math>, a witness test environment <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1}\in E_{\mathrm{test}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1}\in E_{\mathrm{test}}</annotation></semantics></math> with distribution <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{e_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{e_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="((G,X),y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">((G,X),y)</annotation></semantics></math>, and constants <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho&gt;0,L_{h}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho&gt;0,L_{h}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that:
(i) there exists a monotone decreasing <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{\mathrm{fit}}:[0,\infty)\to\mathbb{R}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>fit</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{\mathrm{fit}}:[0,\infty)\to\mathbb{R}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{fit}}(\theta)\geq\psi_{\mathrm{fit}}(\eta_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>fit</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>fit</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{fit}}(\theta)\geq\psi_{\mathrm{fit}}(\eta_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{\mathrm{fit}}(0)&gt;\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>fit</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{\mathrm{fit}}(0)&gt;\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>;
(ii) there exists a monotone decreasing <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{e_{1}}:[0,\infty)\to\mathbb{R}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{e_{1}}:[0,\infty)\to\mathbb{R}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{D_{e_{1}}}[\ell(f_{\theta}(G,X),y)]\geq\psi_{e_{1}}(\eta_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{D_{e_{1}}}[\ell(f_{\theta}(G,X),y)]\geq\psi_{e_{1}}(\eta_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{e_{1}}(0)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{e_{1}}(0)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>;
(iii) admissible perturbations act on the high component, i.e., for <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(G,X)\sim D_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(G,X)\sim D_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}\in B(G,X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}\in B(G,X)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}_{\mathrm{L}}=X_{\mathrm{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">L</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}_{\mathrm{L}}=X_{\mathrm{L}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|X^{\prime}_{\mathrm{H}}-X_{\mathrm{H}}\|\leq\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|X^{\prime}_{\mathrm{H}}-X_{\mathrm{H}}\|\leq\rho</annotation></semantics></math>;
(iv) the head <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz: <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{out}}(h_{\theta}(u),h_{\theta}(v))\leq L_{h}\|u-v\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{out}}(h_{\theta}(u),h_{\theta}(v))\leq L_{h}\|u-v\|</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 3.1 (Witness-family tension under a Lipschitz stability constraint). ‣ 3.2. ℋ_1: A Witness Tension for Static Inference ‣ 3. Problem Formulation and Analysis ‣ Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\max}(\varepsilon):=\varepsilon/(L_{h}\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\max}(\varepsilon):=\varepsilon/(L_{h}\rho)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\min}(\alpha):=\inf\{\eta\geq 0:\psi_{\mathrm{fit}}(\eta)\leq\alpha\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>fit</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\min}(\alpha):=\inf\{\eta\geq 0:\psi_{\mathrm{fit}}(\eta)\leq\alpha\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1 (the constraint caps <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>).</span>
For <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(G,X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(G,X)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}\in B(G,X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}\in B(G,X)</annotation></semantics></math>, Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (High-component necessity and perturbations). ‣ Setup. ‣ Appendix A Proof of the Static-Inference Witness Tension ‣ Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>(iii) gives <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}_{\mathrm{L}}=X_{\mathrm{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}_{\mathrm{L}}=X_{\mathrm{L}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|X^{\prime}_{\mathrm{H}}-X_{\mathrm{H}}\|\leq\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|X^{\prime}_{\mathrm{H}}-X_{\mathrm{H}}\|\leq\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, so the input to <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> differs by at most <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\theta}\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\theta}\rho</annotation></semantics></math>. Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (High-component necessity and perturbations). ‣ Setup. ‣ Appendix A Proof of the Static-Inference Witness Tension ‣ Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>(iv) then yields</p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{X^{\prime}\in B(G,X)}d_{\mathrm{out}}\big(f_{\theta}(G,X),f_{\theta}(G,X^{\prime})\big)\ \leq\ L_{h}\,\eta_{\theta}\,\rho," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{X^{\prime}\in B(G,X)}d_{\mathrm{out}}\big(f_{\theta}(G,X),f_{\theta}(G,X^{\prime})\big)\ \leq\ L_{h}\,\eta_{\theta}\,\rho,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">and hence <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{stab}}(\theta)\leq L_{h}\,\eta_{\theta}\,\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>stab</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{stab}}(\theta)\leq L_{h}\,\eta_{\theta}\,\rho</annotation></semantics></math> in expectation. The Lipschitz stability constraint <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{h}\,\eta_{\theta}\,\rho\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{h}\,\eta_{\theta}\,\rho\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> rearranges to <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\theta}\leq\eta_{\max}(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\theta}\leq\eta_{\max}(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2 (fit forces a minimum <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>).</span>
Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (High-component necessity and perturbations). ‣ Setup. ‣ Appendix A Proof of the Static-Inference Witness Tension ‣ Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>(i) gives <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{fit}}(\theta)\geq\psi_{\mathrm{fit}}(\eta_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>fit</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>fit</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{fit}}(\theta)\geq\psi_{\mathrm{fit}}(\eta_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>. Combined with <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{fit}}(\theta)\leq\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>fit</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{fit}}(\theta)\leq\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, the definition of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\min}(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\min}(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> forces <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\theta}\geq\eta_{\min}(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\theta}\geq\eta_{\min}(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3 (combine).</span>
If <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\min}(\alpha)&gt;\eta_{\max}(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\min}(\alpha)&gt;\eta_{\max}(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>, no <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\mathcal{H}_{1}^{\mathrm{wit}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>wit</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\mathcal{H}_{1}^{\mathrm{wit}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies both constraints. Otherwise <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\theta}\in[\eta_{\min}(\alpha),\eta_{\max}(\varepsilon)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\theta}\in[\eta_{\min}(\alpha),\eta_{\max}(\varepsilon)]</annotation></semantics></math>, and by Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (High-component necessity and perturbations). ‣ Setup. ‣ Appendix A Proof of the Static-Inference Witness Tension ‣ Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>(ii) with <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{e_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{e_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> monotone decreasing,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{ood}}(\theta)\ \geq\ \mathbb{E}_{D_{e_{1}}}\!\big[\ell(f_{\theta}(G,X),y)\big]\ \geq\ \psi_{e_{1}}(\eta_{\theta})\ \geq\ \psi_{e_{1}}\!\big(\eta_{\max}(\varepsilon)\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>ood</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{ood}}(\theta)\ \geq\ \mathbb{E}_{D_{e_{1}}}\!\big[\ell(f_{\theta}(G,X),y)\big]\ \geq\ \psi_{e_{1}}(\eta_{\theta})\ \geq\ \psi_{e_{1}}\!\big(\eta_{\max}(\varepsilon)\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">which is <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> by Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1 (High-component necessity and perturbations). ‣ Setup. ‣ Appendix A Proof of the Static-Inference Witness Tension ‣ Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>(ii).
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proofs for ICC Coverage and Stability Levers</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix proves the two main-text levers, Eq. (<a href="#S3.E10" title="In 3.3. ℋ_2: ICC Exposes Coverage and Stability Levers ‣ 3. Problem Formulation and Analysis ‣ Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) (coverage–selection) and Eq. (<a href="#S3.E11" title="In 3.3. ℋ_2: ICC Exposes Coverage and Stability Levers ‣ 3. Problem Formulation and Analysis ‣ Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>) (stability decomposition).</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1. </span>Coverage-selection bound</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a finite family of mechanisms <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}=\{f^{(k)}\}_{k\in\mathcal{K}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}=\{f^{(k)}\}_{k\in\mathcal{K}}</annotation></semantics></math> and a fixed deterministic discretization <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa:\mathcal{R}\to\mathcal{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa:\mathcal{R}\to\mathcal{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, inducing a discrete selector <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}_{\theta}(z):=\kappa(r_{\theta}(z))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}_{\theta}(z):=\kappa(r_{\theta}(z))</annotation></semantics></math> and a routed predictor <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}(z):=f^{(\tilde{r}_{\theta}(z))}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}(z):=f^{(\tilde{r}_{\theta}(z))}(z)</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in E_{\mathrm{test}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in E_{\mathrm{test}}</annotation></semantics></math>, let</p>
<table id="A2.Ex3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex3X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle k^{\star}(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle k^{\star}(e)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in\arg\min_{k\in\mathcal{K}}\mathbb{E}_{(z,y)\sim D_{e}}[\ell(f^{(k)}(z),y)]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in\arg\min_{k\in\mathcal{K}}\mathbb{E}_{(z,y)\sim D_{e}}[\ell(f^{(k)}(z),y)],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex3Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\delta_{\mathrm{sel}}(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>sel</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta_{\mathrm{sel}}(e)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex3Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\mathbb{P}_{z\sim D_{e}}[\tilde{r}_{\theta}(z)\neq k^{\star}(e)]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\mathbb{P}_{z\sim D_{e}}[\tilde{r}_{\theta}(z)\neq k^{\star}(e)],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\mathrm{cov}}:=\sup_{e\in E_{\mathrm{test}}}\min_{k\in\mathcal{K}}\mathbb{E}_{(z,y)\sim D_{e}}[\ell(f^{(k)}(z),y)]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\mathrm{cov}}:=\sup_{e\in E_{\mathrm{test}}}\min_{k\in\mathcal{K}}\mathbb{E}_{(z,y)\sim D_{e}}[\ell(f^{(k)}(z),y)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We assume the evaluation loss is bounded: <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\ell\leq L_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\ell\leq L_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> on the support of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup_{e\in E_{\mathrm{test}}}D_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup_{e\in E_{\mathrm{test}}}D_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> (training may still use an unbounded surrogate).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Eq. (<a href="#S3.E10" title="In 3.3. ℋ_2: ICC Exposes Coverage and Stability Levers ‣ 3. Problem Formulation and Analysis ‣ Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>).</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Pointwise, for any <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(z,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(z,y)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\in E_{\mathrm{test}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\in E_{\mathrm{test}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\ell(f_{\theta}(z),y)\ \leq\ \ell\big(f^{(k^{\star}(e))}(z),y\big)+L_{\max}\,\mathbf{1}\{\tilde{r}_{\theta}(z)\neq k^{\star}(e)\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell(f_{\theta}(z),y)\ \leq\ \ell\big(f^{(k^{\star}(e))}(z),y\big)+L_{\max}\,\mathbf{1}\{\tilde{r}_{\theta}(z)\neq k^{\star}(e)\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">since the indicator switches on iff the selected mechanism differs from <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\star}(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\star}(e)</annotation></semantics></math>, and the loss is bounded by <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking expectation under <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{e}</annotation></semantics></math> and using the definitions of <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\mathrm{cov}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\mathrm{cov}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\mathrm{sel}}(e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>sel</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\mathrm{sel}}(e)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{(z,y)\sim D_{e}}[\ell(f_{\theta}(z),y)]\ \leq\ \beta_{\mathrm{cov}}+L_{\max}\,\delta_{\mathrm{sel}}(e)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>sel</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{(z,y)\sim D_{e}}[\ell(f_{\theta}(z),y)]\ \leq\ \beta_{\mathrm{cov}}+L_{\max}\,\delta_{\mathrm{sel}}(e).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{e\in E_{\mathrm{test}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>test</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{e\in E_{\mathrm{test}}}</annotation></semantics></math> yields Eq. (<a href="#S3.E10" title="In 3.3. ℋ_2: ICC Exposes Coverage and Stability Levers ‣ 3. Problem Formulation and Analysis ‣ Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2. </span>Stability decomposition</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Equip <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> with a distance <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{dist}_{\mathcal{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>dist</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{dist}_{\mathcal{R}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the routing-fixed sensitivity and routing drift</p>
<table id="A2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{base}}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim D_{0}}\!\Big[\sup_{z^{\prime}\in B(z)}d_{\mathrm{out}}\big(F(r_{\theta}(z),z),F(r_{\theta}(z),z^{\prime})\big)\Big]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>base</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{base}}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim D_{0}}\!\Big[\sup_{z^{\prime}\in B(z)}d_{\mathrm{out}}\big(F(r_{\theta}(z),z),F(r_{\theta}(z),z^{\prime})\big)\Big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{route}}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim D_{0}}\!\Big[\sup_{z^{\prime}\in B(z)}\mathrm{dist}_{\mathcal{R}}\big(r_{\theta}(z),r_{\theta}(z^{\prime})\big)\Big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>route</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>dist</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{route}}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim D_{0}}\!\Big[\sup_{z^{\prime}\in B(z)}\mathrm{dist}_{\mathcal{R}}\big(r_{\theta}(z),r_{\theta}(z^{\prime})\big)\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let the pointwise routing envelope and the uniform envelope (assumed finite) be</p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{F}(z):=\sup_{\begin{subarray}{c}r,r^{\prime}\in\mathcal{R}\\
\mathrm{dist}_{\mathcal{R}}(r,r^{\prime})&gt;0\end{subarray}}\frac{d_{\mathrm{out}}(F(r,z),F(r^{\prime},z))}{\mathrm{dist}_{\mathcal{R}}(r,r^{\prime})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>dist</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>dist</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{F}(z):=\sup_{\begin{subarray}{c}r,r^{\prime}\in\mathcal{R}\\
\mathrm{dist}_{\mathcal{R}}(r,r^{\prime})&gt;0\end{subarray}}\frac{d_{\mathrm{out}}(F(r,z),F(r^{\prime},z))}{\mathrm{dist}_{\mathcal{R}}(r,r^{\prime})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{F}^{B}(D_{0}):=\sup_{z\in\mathrm{supp}(D_{0})}\ \sup_{z^{\prime}\in B(z)}L_{F}(z^{\prime})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>F</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{F}^{B}(D_{0}):=\sup_{z\in\mathrm{supp}(D_{0})}\ \sup_{z^{\prime}\in B(z)}L_{F}(z^{\prime}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Eq. (<a href="#S3.E11" title="In 3.3. ℋ_2: ICC Exposes Coverage and Stability Levers ‣ 3. Problem Formulation and Analysis ‣ Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>).</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\sim D_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\sim D_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and any <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{\prime}\in B(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{\prime}\in B(z)</annotation></semantics></math>. Write <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=r_{\theta}(z),r^{\prime}=r_{\theta}(z^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=r_{\theta}(z),r^{\prime}=r_{\theta}(z^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. By triangle inequality,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{out}}\big(F(r,z),F(r^{\prime},z^{\prime})\big)\ \leq\ d_{\mathrm{out}}\big(F(r,z),F(r,z^{\prime})\big)\ +\ d_{\mathrm{out}}\big(F(r,z^{\prime}),F(r^{\prime},z^{\prime})\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{out}}\big(F(r,z),F(r^{\prime},z^{\prime})\big)\ \leq\ d_{\mathrm{out}}\big(F(r,z),F(r,z^{\prime})\big)\ +\ d_{\mathrm{out}}\big(F(r,z^{\prime}),F(r^{\prime},z^{\prime})\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">The pointwise envelope gives <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{out}}(F(r,z^{\prime}),F(r^{\prime},z^{\prime}))\leq L_{F}(z^{\prime})\,\mathrm{dist}_{\mathcal{R}}(r,r^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>out</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>dist</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{out}}(F(r,z^{\prime}),F(r^{\prime},z^{\prime}))\leq L_{F}(z^{\prime})\,\mathrm{dist}_{\mathcal{R}}(r,r^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>. Taking <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{z^{\prime}\in B(z)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{z^{\prime}\in B(z)}</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{z\sim D_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{z\sim D_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the first term yields <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{base}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>base</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{base}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{F}^{B}(D_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>F</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{F}^{B}(D_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> is a uniform constant over <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{supp}(D_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{supp}(D_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, it factors out of the expectation, and the second term is bounded by <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{F}^{B}(D_{0})\,\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{route}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>F</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mi>route</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{F}^{B}(D_{0})\,\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{route}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proofs for VQ and Lipschitz Control</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1. </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 4.1 (Margin-based invariance of the VQ interface). ‣ 4.2. Stabilizing Intermediate Representations via VQ Tokenization ‣ 4. Methodology ‣ Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix an input <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> and a node <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j^{\star}:=q_{\theta}(v;z)=\arg\min_{1\leq j\leq M}\|u_{v}(z)-c_{j}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j^{\star}:=q_{\theta}(v;z)=\arg\min_{1\leq j\leq M}\|u_{v}(z)-c_{j}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Recall the margin</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{v}(z):=\min_{j\neq j^{\star}}\|u_{v}(z)-c_{j}\|_{2}-\|u_{v}(z)-c_{j^{\star}}\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{v}(z):=\min_{j\neq j^{\star}}\|u_{v}(z)-c_{j}\|_{2}-\|u_{v}(z)-c_{j^{\star}}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Fix any <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{\prime}\in B(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{\prime}\in B(z)</annotation></semantics></math> and set <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta:=\|u_{v}(z^{\prime})-u_{v}(z)\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>:=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta:=\|u_{v}(z^{\prime})-u_{v}(z)\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>; by assumption, <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&lt;\tfrac{1}{2}m_{v}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&lt;\tfrac{1}{2}m_{v}(z)</annotation></semantics></math>. Triangle inequality gives, for any competitor <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq j^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq j^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex13X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex13X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|u_{v}(z^{\prime})-c_{j^{\star}}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|u_{v}(z^{\prime})-c_{j^{\star}}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex13X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\|u_{v}(z)-c_{j^{\star}}\|_{2}+\delta," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\|u_{v}(z)-c_{j^{\star}}\|_{2}+\delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex13Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex13Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|u_{v}(z^{\prime})-c_{j}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|u_{v}(z^{\prime})-c_{j}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex13Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\|u_{v}(z)-c_{j}\|_{2}-\delta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\|u_{v}(z)-c_{j}\|_{2}-\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|u_{v}(z^{\prime})-c_{j}\|_{2}-\|u_{v}(z^{\prime})-c_{j^{\star}}\|_{2}\geq m_{v}(z)-2\delta&gt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|u_{v}(z^{\prime})-c_{j}\|_{2}-\|u_{v}(z^{\prime})-c_{j^{\star}}\|_{2}\geq m_{v}(z)-2\delta&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">so the nearest-code assignment is unchanged: <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\theta}(v;z^{\prime})=j^{\star}=q_{\theta}(v;z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta}(v;z^{\prime})=j^{\star}=q_{\theta}(v;z)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since this holds for every <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math> and every <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{\prime}\in B(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{\prime}\in B(z)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(u_{\theta}(z^{\prime}))=Q(u_{\theta}(z))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(u_{\theta}(z^{\prime}))=Q(u_{\theta}(z))</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{\prime}\in B(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{\prime}\in B(z)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2. </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition 4.2 (Bounded output amplification under token switches). ‣ 4.3. Bounding Output Amplification via Lipschitz Regularization ‣ 4. Methodology ‣ Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}=\{c_{j}\}_{j=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}=\{c_{j}\}_{j=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> be the VQ codebook (the implementation uses grouped <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>-head VQ with <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H{=}4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H{=}4</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> then denotes the concatenated per-head token space, and the invariance condition in Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 4.1 (Margin-based invariance of the VQ interface). ‣ 4.2. Stabilizing Intermediate Representations via VQ Tokenization ‣ 4. Methodology ‣ Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> is applied per head) and define its diameter</p>
<table id="A3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{diam}(\mathcal{C}):=\max_{i,j}\|c_{i}-c_{j}\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>diam</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{diam}(\mathcal{C}):=\max_{i,j}\|c_{i}-c_{j}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let the token embedding for node <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{u}_{v}(z)=Q(u_{v}(z))\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{u}_{v}(z)=Q(u_{v}(z))\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Node-level tasks (no pooling).</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{\prime}\in B(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{\prime}\in B(z)</annotation></semantics></math> and any node <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, both <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{u}_{v}(z^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{u}_{v}(z^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{u}_{v}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{u}_{v}(z)</annotation></semantics></math> lie in <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence</p>
<table id="A3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\tilde{u}_{v}(z^{\prime})-\tilde{u}_{v}(z)\|_{2}\leq\mathrm{diam}(\mathcal{C})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>diam</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\tilde{u}_{v}(z^{\prime})-\tilde{u}_{v}(z)\|_{2}\leq\mathrm{diam}(\mathcal{C}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Since the head is <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz under <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{t}(\tilde{u}_{v}(z^{\prime}))-f_{t}(\tilde{u}_{v}(z))\|_{2}\leq L\|\tilde{u}_{v}(z^{\prime})-\tilde{u}_{v}(z)\|_{2}\leq L\,\mathrm{diam}(\mathcal{C})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diam</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{t}(\tilde{u}_{v}(z^{\prime}))-f_{t}(\tilde{u}_{v}(z))\|_{2}\leq L\|\tilde{u}_{v}(z^{\prime})-\tilde{u}_{v}(z)\|_{2}\leq L\,\mathrm{diam}(\mathcal{C}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Graph-level tasks (with pooling).</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(z)=\{\tilde{u}_{v}(z)\}_{v\in V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(z)=\{\tilde{u}_{v}(z)\}_{v\in V}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the token set.
Assume the pooling operator is <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathrm{pool}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>pool</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathrm{pool}}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz with respect to the nodewise norm</p>
<table id="A3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|A\|_{V,2}:=\Big(\frac{1}{|V|}\sum_{v\in V}\|a_{v}\|_{2}^{2}\Big)^{1/2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|A\|_{V,2}:=\Big(\frac{1}{|V|}\sum_{v\in V}\|a_{v}\|_{2}^{2}\Big)^{1/2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">namely,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathrm{Pool}(A)-\mathrm{Pool}(B)\|_{2}\leq L_{\mathrm{pool}}\|A-B\|_{V,2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Pool</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>Pool</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>pool</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathrm{Pool}(A)-\mathrm{Pool}(B)\|_{2}\leq L_{\mathrm{pool}}\|A-B\|_{V,2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The per-node bound <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\tilde{u}_{v}(z^{\prime})-\tilde{u}_{v}(z)\|_{2}\leq\mathrm{diam}(\mathcal{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>diam</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\tilde{u}_{v}(z^{\prime})-\tilde{u}_{v}(z)\|_{2}\leq\mathrm{diam}(\mathcal{C})</annotation></semantics></math> implies</p>
<table id="A3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|A(z^{\prime})-A(z)\|_{V,2}\leq\mathrm{diam}(\mathcal{C})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>diam</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|A(z^{\prime})-A(z)\|_{V,2}\leq\mathrm{diam}(\mathcal{C}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(z)=\mathrm{Pool}(A(z))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pool</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(z)=\mathrm{Pool}(A(z))</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="A3.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|r(z^{\prime})-r(z)\|_{2}\leq L_{\mathrm{pool}}\,\mathrm{diam}(\mathcal{C})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>pool</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diam</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|r(z^{\prime})-r(z)\|_{2}\leq L_{\mathrm{pool}}\,\mathrm{diam}(\mathcal{C}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">and by the <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitzness of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{t}(r(z^{\prime}))-f_{t}(r(z))\|_{2}\leq L\|r(z^{\prime})-r(z)\|_{2}\leq L\,L_{\mathrm{pool}}\,\mathrm{diam}(\mathcal{C})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>pool</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>diam</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{t}(r(z^{\prime}))-f_{t}(r(z))\|_{2}\leq L\|r(z^{\prime})-r(z)\|_{2}\leq L\,L_{\mathrm{pool}}\,\mathrm{diam}(\mathcal{C}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">This matches Eq. (<a href="#S4.E23" title="In Proposition 4.2 (Bounded output amplification under token switches). ‣ 4.3. Bounding Output Amplification via Lipschitz Regularization ‣ 4. Methodology ‣ Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>) (<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\mathrm{pool}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>pool</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\mathrm{pool}}=1</annotation></semantics></math> recovers the node-level bound).
∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Experimental Details</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1. </span>Routing Specialization and VQ Stability</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Panel (a) splits WikiCS test nodes by local feature homophily (<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\leq 0.33" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.33</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\leq 0.33</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h&gt;0.67" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.67</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h&gt;0.67</annotation></semantics></math>): Expert-0 drops <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="62\%{\to}46\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>62</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>46</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">62\%{\to}46\%</annotation></semantics></math> and Expert-2 rises <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="25\%{\to}43\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>25</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>43</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">25\%{\to}43\%</annotation></semantics></math>, an <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="18" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>18</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">18</annotation></semantics></math>-point top-1 swing that rules out router collapse and supports the coverage mechanism behind <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{\mathrm{cov}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>cov</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{\mathrm{cov}}</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <a href="#S3.E10" title="In 3.3. ℋ_2: ICC Exposes Coverage and Stability Levers ‣ 3. Problem Formulation and Analysis ‣ Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>. Panel (b) reports the per-head mean codebook margin against the switch rate at <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p{=}0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p{=}0.1</annotation></semantics></math> as a descriptive summary; across the three datasets larger mean margin coincides with lower switch rate (WikiCS <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.62" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.62</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.62</annotation></semantics></math> / <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6.2\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6.2</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6.2\%</annotation></semantics></math>; PubMed <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.29" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.29</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.29</annotation></semantics></math> / <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15.4\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>15.4</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15.4\%</annotation></semantics></math>). Consistent with the per-head mechanism of Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 4.1 (Margin-based invariance of the VQ interface). ‣ 4.2. Stabilizing Intermediate Representations via VQ Tokenization ‣ 4. Methodology ‣ Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, the sufficient invariance bound is governed by the minimum-margin head; the mean is shown only as a coarse aggregate and is not the quantity the lemma controls. The residual amplification of these switches is bounded by the Lipschitz penalty (Eq. <a href="#S4.E22" title="In 4.3. Bounding Output Amplification via Lipschitz Regularization ‣ 4. Methodology ‣ Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) on the prediction head.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.09258v2/routing_switch.svg" id="A4.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/212;" width="476" height="212"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>. </span><span id="A4.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Mechanism diagnostics. (a) Top-1 expert distribution on WikiCS, split by local feature homophily. (b) Per-dataset per-head mean codebook margin vs. token switch rate at <math id="A4.F6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p{=}0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p{=}0.1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2. </span>Additional Ablation Studies</h3>

<section id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Joint VQ and Lipschitz ablation under perturbation.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We jointly remove both the VQ codebook and the Lipschitz penalty from STEM-GNN, retaining only the MoE encoder (<em id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Vanilla MoE</em>, w/o VQ &amp; Lip), and evaluate on Cora and PubMed under feature masking at <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\{0.5,0.6\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\{0.5,0.6\}</annotation></semantics></math> (Table <a href="#A4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Joint VQ and Lipschitz ablation under perturbation. ‣ D.2. Additional Ablation Studies ‣ Appendix D Experimental Details ‣ Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). The gap widens sharply with masking severity (<math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2.29" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2.29</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2.29</annotation></semantics></math> / <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2.67" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2.67</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2.67</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha{=}0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha{=}0.6</annotation></semantics></math> on Cora / PubMed), supporting that VQ and Lipschitz jointly bound the amplification of perturbation-induced representation and token-switch variation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A4.T5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>. </span><span id="A4.T5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Joint ablation of VQ and Lipschitz under feature masking. Numbers are node-classification accuracy (%); <math id="A4.T5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is Vanilla MoE minus STEM-GNN.</span></figcaption>
