</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3. </span>Additional Diagnostics</h3>

<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Compute and parameter footprint.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On Cora (NVIDIA L40), STEM-GNN trains at <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5.24{\pm}0.04" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5.24</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.04</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5.24{\pm}0.04</annotation></semantics></math> ms/epoch and infers at <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.72{\pm}0.09" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.72</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.09</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.72{\pm}0.09</annotation></semantics></math> ms/pass with <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="279" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>279</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">279</annotation></semantics></math> MB peak memory. The model has <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9.93" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9.93</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9.93</annotation></semantics></math> M parameters versus <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7.57" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7.57</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7.57</annotation></semantics></math> M for GFT; the <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}3</annotation></semantics></math> MoE router is a single linear layer (<math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.3</annotation></semantics></math> K params), and the Lipschitz penalty is loss-only (<math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> params). Soft routing (Eq. <a href="#S4.E14" title="In 4.1. Coverage Expansion via MoE Encoder ‣ 4. Methodology ‣ Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) evaluates all experts in one forward pass, avoiding top-<math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> dispatch overheads of sparse MoE.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Statistical reliability and sensitivity.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the tri-objective evaluation, <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50/60" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50/60</annotation></semantics></math> comparisons against five baselines show large effects (<math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|d|&gt;0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|d|&gt;0.8</annotation></semantics></math>), with <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="47/50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>47</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">47/50</annotation></semantics></math> of these having <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="95\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">95\%</annotation></semantics></math> confidence intervals excluding zero. Sensitivity sweeps show only modest variation: changing the routing temperature <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in[0.3,2.0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in[0.3,2.0]</annotation></semantics></math> on WikiCS changes OOD accuracy by <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;1.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;1.3</annotation></semantics></math> pp, and changing the Lipschitz coefficient <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{lip}}\in[0,10^{-2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>lip</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{lip}}\in[0,10^{-2}]</annotation></semantics></math> on Cora changes it by <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;1.0</annotation></semantics></math> pp.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Per-dataset perturbation results.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A4.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Per-dataset perturbation results. ‣ D.3. Additional Diagnostics ‣ Appendix D Experimental Details ‣ Generalizing GNNs with Tokenized Mixture of Experts" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> reports the remaining perturbation settings (PubMed/WikiCS feature masking, Cora/ WikiCS edge deletion); STEM-GNN stays the most stable across all panels and severities (<math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\{0.4,0.5,0.6\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\{0.4,0.5,0.6\}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.09258v2/noise_appendix.svg" id="A4.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/414;" width="476" height="414"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>. </span><span id="A4.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Stability under inference-time perturbation (accuracy, %) across feature masking and edge deletion.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4. </span>Hyperparameters</h3>

<section id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Pre-training.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The encoder is a two-layer GraphSAGE backbone (hidden <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="768" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>768</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">768</annotation></semantics></math>, ReLU, batch normalization, dropout <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.15</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.15</annotation></semantics></math>) with a vector-quantized token interface (codebook <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M{=}128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>128</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M{=}128</annotation></semantics></math>, dim <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="768" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>768</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">768</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> grouped heads, commitment weight <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math>) and a last-layer MoE of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}3</annotation></semantics></math> experts with Gumbel-Softmax routing (<math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau{=}1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau{=}1.0</annotation></semantics></math>). Pre-training minimizes three objectives on the tokenized representations—node-feature reconstruction, link reconstruction over <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\%</annotation></semantics></math> held-out edges, and semantic alignment—together with the VQ commitment loss, using feature masking and edge dropping (rate <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.2</annotation></semantics></math>). We optimize with AdamW (lr <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\mathrm{e}{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\mathrm{e}{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, weight decay <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\mathrm{e}{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\mathrm{e}{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, cosine schedule) for <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>25</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">25</annotation></semantics></math> epochs at batch size <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1024</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1024</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Fine-tuning.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We fine-tune with AdamW for frozen deployment: the VQ codebook is frozen (<span id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">freeze_vq=1</span>), the last-layer MoE encoder (<math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}3</annotation></semantics></math>) and a linear, Lipschitz-regularized head are optimized, and checkpoints are selected by validation accuracy. Batch normalization is used for link/graph tasks and disabled for node tasks.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</article>
